[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113499,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "<p>Sclerosing polycystic adenoma (SPA) is a circumscribed salivary gland neoplasm composed of large acinar cells with brightly eosinophilic intracytoplasmic granules, and variable ductal and cystic components, including foamy, vacuolated, and apocrine cells.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:47:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113500,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8140/0 Sclerosing polycystic adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113501,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E91.Z Benign neoplasm of unspecified major salivary glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113502,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> sclerosing polycystic adenosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113503,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113504,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The majority (80%) arise in the parotid gland, with occasional sinonasal, submandibular, and lacrimal gland involvement {16434888; 17150380; 20549092; 20614339; 23465282; 23552085; 34510113}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113505,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SPA is a slow-growing, painless mass. It is rarely multifocal {16434888; 21286874; 24636837}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113506,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SPA is rare {16434888}. The mean age at presentation is 40&nbsp;years (range: 7&ndash;84&nbsp;years), and there is a slight female predominance {28614209}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113507,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rare cases are associated with polycystic/dysgenetic disease {32031136} and Cowden syndrome {34410594}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113508,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SPA was originally regarded as pseudoneoplastic {8554105; 11942573}, until monoclonality was demonstrated by polymorphism of human androgen receptor assay {16861963}. Consistent mutations in PI3K pathway genes, most frequently <em>PTEN</em>, confirm its neoplastic nature and suggest links with apocrine intraductal carcinoma and salivary duct carcinoma {31605313; 31989433; 33526220; 34410594; 34510113}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113509,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SPA is a well-circumscribed, often encapsulated nodule measuring 10&ndash;120&nbsp;mm (mean: 30&nbsp;mm). The cut section is partially solid and cystic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113510,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SPA is characterized by a cystic and multilobular pattern, composed of variably sized and shaped ducts lined by flattened, cylindrical, or apocrine foamy or vacuolated epithelium, embedded in a sclerotic collagenous stroma with focal lymphoid aggregates {28060365; 28614209; 33526220}. The hallmark of SPA is the presence of acini containing large, brightly eosinophilic cytoplasmic granules/globules. SPA often display solid, cribriform, and micropapillary proliferations with variable degrees of cytological atypia, surrounded by myoepithelial cells, resembling intraductal carcinoma {23821217}. SPA is rarely associated with invasive carcinoma {24584973; 34410594; 34510113}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Each cellular component demonstrates its expected immunophenotype: SOX10 in ductules, myoepithelial cells, and acini; SMA, p40, and calponin in myoepithelial cells; and AR and GCDFP-15 in apocrine cells. There is frequent loss of PTEN in ductal and acinar cells, but not in myoepithelial cells {31605313; 34410594}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113511,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears show a mix of flat, cohesive sheets of epithelial cells with variably granular oncocytic cytoplasm and round nuclei; sheets of apocrine-type epithelium; and histiocytic cells in a proteinaceous background. The coexistence of different cell types in a single sheet is helpful {17580340; 19937766; 28060365}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113512,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113513,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> mixtures of ductal and myoepithelial cells, with acinar cells containing large hypereosinophilic cytoplasmic granules.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> apocrine metaplasia and intraductal proliferation creating a resemblance to low-grade ductal carcinoma in&nbsp;situ; cystic appearance; PTEN loss by immunohistochemistry (in selected cases).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-22T14:18:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113514,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113515,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 74,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is local recurrence in 10% of incompletely excised or multifocal cases {8554105; 11942573; 23821217; 24595421; 33526220}. Rare invasive carcinomas ex SPA have been reported {24584973; 34510113}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:20:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]